# Build context here is this directory (docker-compose.yml ->
# ultron-discord-bot service), and its Dockerfile does "COPY . ." — a
# broad copy, so unlike the backend's this file is the only thing keeping
# stray local files (a .env someone drops here for local testing, venv/,
# __pycache__/) out of the image.

# ==============================================================================
# 1. DENY-BY-DEFAULT (ignore everything first)
# ==============================================================================
**

# ==============================================================================
# 2. ALLOWLIST — exactly what this Dockerfile needs: requirements.txt,
#    every .py module (just bot.py today, but any future module too),
#    and the README for anyone shelling into the running container.
# ==============================================================================
!*.py
!requirements.txt
!README.md

# ==============================================================================
# 3. EXPLICIT BLOCKS
# ==============================================================================
**/.env*
**/.claude/
**/.git/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/venv/
**/.venv/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
